#: ../../benchmarks.rst:1229
msgid ""
"**Like for like.** The HAProxy file of the tables above adds no header to "
"a request. Sibuna always adds seven: ``X-Forwarded-For``, "
"``X-Forwarded-Proto``, ``X-Forwarded-Host``, ``X-Forwarded-Port``, "
"``X-Real-IP``, ``X-Sibuna-Status`` and ``X-Sibuna-Rule``. So HAProxy did "
"less work for each request. We gave HAProxy ``option forwardfor`` and six "
"``http-request set-header`` lines that write the same seven headers, and "
"measured both again on one host with 256 connections for six seconds. "
"Both proxies negotiated TLS 1.3 with ``TLS_AES_256_GCM_SHA384`` and the "
"same ECDSA P-256 certificate, and both ran on the same eight CPUs."
msgstr ""
"**Gleiches mit Gleichem.** Die HAProxy-Datei der obigen Tabellen fügt "
"einer Anfrage keinen Header hinzu. Sibuna fügt immer sieben hinzu: "
"``X-Forwarded-For``, ``X-Forwarded-Proto``, ``X-Forwarded-Host``, "
"``X-Forwarded-Port``, ``X-Real-IP``, ``X-Sibuna-Status`` und "
"``X-Sibuna-Rule``. HAProxy leistete also für jede Anfrage weniger Arbeit. "
"Wir haben HAProxy ``option forwardfor`` und sechs ``http-request "
"set-header``-Zeilen gegeben, die dieselben sieben Header schreiben, und "
"beide erneut auf einem Host mit 256 Verbindungen sechs Sekunden lang "
"gemessen. Beide Proxys handelten TLS 1.3 mit ``TLS_AES_256_GCM_SHA384`` "
"und demselben ECDSA-P-256-Zertifikat aus, und beide liefen auf denselben "
"acht CPUs."

